{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Machinery.HeckeTauAssignmentCoherence","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Machinery.HeckeTauAssignmentCoherence","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Machinery.HeckeTauAssignmentCanonicity"],"declarations":10,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.CoxeterParabolic.tauAssignment_flip_coherent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.CoxeterParabolic.tauAssignment_flip_coherent","kind":"theorem","line":167,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/HeckeTauAssignmentCoherence.lean#L167-L179","doc":"**The flip edge at A₃**: the `(2,1)`-assignment is the pullback of\nthe `(0,1)`-assignment along the flip automorphism — the two braid\npairs of the A₃ diagram carry coherently-identified assignments, even\nthough (by `tauAssignment_pair_dependent`) the assignments themselves\nare distinct functions. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.CoxeterParabolic.flipA3_symm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.CoxeterParabolic.flipA3_symm","kind":"theorem","line":163,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/HeckeTauAssignmentCoherence.lean#L163-L165","doc":"The A₃ matrix is flip-symmetric. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.CoxeterParabolic.flipA3","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.CoxeterParabolic.flipA3","kind":"def","line":156,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/HeckeTauAssignmentCoherence.lean#L156-L161","doc":"The A₃ diagram automorphism `0 ↔ 2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.CoxeterParabolic.tauAssignment_diagram_coherent_bar","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.CoxeterParabolic.tauAssignment_diagram_coherent_bar","kind":"theorem","line":137,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/HeckeTauAssignmentCoherence.lean#L137-L152","doc":"The conjugate `H^{0,1}` partner square. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.CoxeterParabolic.tauAssignment_diagram_coherent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.CoxeterParabolic.tauAssignment_diagram_coherent","kind":"theorem","line":117,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/HeckeTauAssignmentCoherence.lean#L117-L135","doc":"**Diagram symmetries intertwine the τ-assignments**: the assignment\nat the image pair is the pullback of the assignment at the source pair\nalong the induced endomorphism. The first proved edge of the coherence\ngroupoid. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.CoxeterParabolic.cellElem3_diagramHom","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.CoxeterParabolic.cellElem3_diagramHom","kind":"theorem","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/HeckeTauAssignmentCoherence.lean#L90-L113","doc":"The six-element cell of the image pair is the `diagramHom`-image of\nthe cell of the source pair. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.CoxeterParabolic.simple_ne_map","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.CoxeterParabolic.simple_ne_map","kind":"theorem","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/HeckeTauAssignmentCoherence.lean#L82-L86","doc":"Simple-distinctness transports along any bijection of the index\nset — supplied unconditionally by the Chebyshev leg. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.CoxeterParabolic.diagramHom_simple","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.CoxeterParabolic.diagramHom_simple","kind":"theorem","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/HeckeTauAssignmentCoherence.lean#L77-L80","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.CoxeterParabolic.diagramHom","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.CoxeterParabolic.diagramHom","kind":"def","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/HeckeTauAssignmentCoherence.lean#L71-L75","doc":"The group endomorphism `σ k ↦ σ (e k)` induced by a matrix\nsymmetry. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Machinery.CoxeterParabolic.diagramLiftable","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Machinery.CoxeterParabolic.diagramLiftable","kind":"theorem","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Machinery/HeckeTauAssignmentCoherence.lean#L63-L69","doc":"A matrix symmetry makes the shifted simple-selection liftable: the\nCoxeter relations transport along `e`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}